-- title:
--   Integrality of Y^{2N}ĵ^{N+1}(ĵ-1728)^N over ℂ[ĵ⁻¹]
-- statement:
--   Fix a positive integer $N$, a cusp form $f$ of weight $2$ for $\Gamma_0(N)$, and a Laurent series $Y \in \mathbb{C}((q))$. Write $\hat{j} :=$ `coeffEmb ℂ jq` for the image in $\mathbb{C}((q))$, under the coefficientwise ring map induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to \mathbb{C}$, of the rational Laurent series `jq` $= q^{-1}\cdot$ (the power series `jNum` with its coefficients mapped from $\mathbb{Z}$ to $\mathbb{Q}$); and let $\theta$ denote the $\mathbb{C}$-linear operator `thetaL ℂ` on $\mathbb{C}((q))$ sending $g$ to $q \cdot g'$, i.e. multiplication by the monomial $q^{1}$ composed with the formal derivative. Assume $Y \cdot \theta(\hat{j})$ equals the $q$-expansion of $f$ at width $1$, viewed as an element of $\mathbb{C}((q))$ through the inclusion of formal power series into Laurent series. The conclusion is that the Laurent series $Y^{2N}\,\hat{j}^{\,N+1}\,(\hat{j}-1728)^{N}$ is integral over the $\mathbb{C}$-subalgebra of $\mathbb{C}((q))$ generated by the single element $\hat{j}^{-1}$.
--
--   This is the integrality statement behind the classical fact that, for $f \in S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ and $\theta \hat{j} = -E_4^2E_6/\Delta$, the function $f^{2N}E_4^{3-N}/\Delta$ is a modular function for $\Gamma_0(N)$ whose transforms have elementary symmetric functions polynomial in $1/j$. It is used in [`ModularCurve.one_sub_ord_le_ord_of_coeffMap_mul_thetaL_eq_qExpansion`](thm.html#ModularCurve.one_sub_ord_le_ord_of_coeffMap_mul_thetaL_eq_qExpansion) to bound the $q$-order of $Y$, and its proof invokes the expansions of $E_4$, $E_6$, $\Delta$ and $j$ recorded in [`ModularCurve.jqModC_eq_qExpansion_E4_cube_div_discriminant`](thm.html#ModularCurve.jqModC_eq_qExpansion_E4_cube_div_discriminant), [`omegaRow_T2`](thm.html#omegaRow_T2) and [`ModularForm.exists_qExpansion_eq_aeval_mul_pow_levelOne`](thm.html#ModularForm.exists_qExpansion_eq_aeval_mul_pow_levelOne).
-- source:
